1
00:00:25,926 --> 00:00:28,159
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,303
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,449 --> 00:00:51,449
♪ ♪

4
00:01:13,773 --> 00:01:17,709
♪ ♪

5
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:51,175
♪ ♪

6
00:02:21,608 --> 00:02:23,486
Among the things
we still don't know

7
00:02:23,510 --> 00:02:26,211
is why famed defense
attorney Benjamin Matlock,

8
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,880
who entered the
prison five days ago,

9
00:02:28,949 --> 00:02:30,949
still has yet to leave.

10
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:33,718
Is he a negotiator, a hostage

11
00:02:33,787 --> 00:02:37,188
or is he defending the
guard on trial for murder?

12
00:02:37,258 --> 00:02:40,058
Oh, yes, sir, he is.

13
00:02:40,127 --> 00:02:42,261
It's the governor.

14
00:02:42,329 --> 00:02:44,730
Yes.

15
00:02:44,798 --> 00:02:48,166
He was found
hanging in his cell.

16
00:02:48,235 --> 00:02:49,879
I can't tell you anything else.

17
00:02:49,903 --> 00:02:52,003
Looked like suicide.

18
00:02:52,072 --> 00:02:53,950
Ben says it looked
like a suicide.

19
00:02:53,974 --> 00:02:55,240
Only it wasn't suicide.

20
00:02:55,309 --> 00:02:59,378
Only he says it
wasn't a suicide.

21
00:02:59,446 --> 00:03:00,912
You sure about that?

22
00:03:00,981 --> 00:03:02,281
Positive.

23
00:03:02,349 --> 00:03:06,017
He's positive, Governor.

24
00:03:06,086 --> 00:03:09,120
I understand.

25
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:11,656
Well, I know that, but...

26
00:03:14,828 --> 00:03:17,362
Wait a minute. Please hold on.

27
00:03:17,431 --> 00:03:19,597
He's afraid if he
doesn't respond

28
00:03:19,666 --> 00:03:22,533
to this second killing
with some show of force,

29
00:03:22,603 --> 00:03:24,536
that the press will crucify him

30
00:03:24,605 --> 00:03:25,938
when they find out about it.

31
00:03:26,006 --> 00:03:27,706
He can't do that.

32
00:03:27,775 --> 00:03:31,276
The warden doesn't
think that's a good idea

33
00:03:31,344 --> 00:03:32,811
and frankly, neither do I.

34
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:35,447
Tell him... Give me the phone.

35
00:03:36,783 --> 00:03:39,584
Just give me the phone.

36
00:03:39,653 --> 00:03:43,021
Burt, Ben Matlock.

37
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:46,758
Now listen, I know
it doesn't sound like

38
00:03:46,827 --> 00:03:49,694
we're making much
progress, but we are.

39
00:03:49,763 --> 00:03:53,464
I can't do it in 48 hours.

40
00:03:53,534 --> 00:03:55,834
And they won't
let me out of here.

41
00:03:55,903 --> 00:03:58,069
I've got to have more time.

42
00:04:00,274 --> 00:04:02,641
I understand.

43
00:04:02,709 --> 00:04:05,477
I understand.

44
00:04:05,546 --> 00:04:08,613
And here's something
for you to understand...

45
00:04:08,682 --> 00:04:11,416
I'm in this and
I've got to finish,

46
00:04:11,485 --> 00:04:14,052
or there's going to be
a lot more dead people,

47
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,753
and I might be one of them,

48
00:04:15,822 --> 00:04:17,622
and I'm too damn young to die.

49
00:04:17,691 --> 00:04:19,658
You got that?

50
00:04:19,726 --> 00:04:23,295
I don't know what to tell
you to do with the press.

51
00:04:23,363 --> 00:04:25,230
I know... lie.

52
00:04:25,299 --> 00:04:27,332
48 hours!

53
00:04:27,401 --> 00:04:29,368
Anything I can do?

54
00:04:29,436 --> 00:04:30,535
I don't know.

55
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:31,769
Yes.

56
00:04:31,839 --> 00:04:35,140
Transfer Rudy Chambers
to Greenwood Prison.

57
00:04:35,208 --> 00:04:37,175
Rudy Chambers is dead.

58
00:04:37,244 --> 00:04:38,309
Maybe not.

59
00:04:43,751 --> 00:04:46,651
You'll be given a
daily work assignment.

60
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,919
Only when it's complete

61
00:04:47,988 --> 00:04:50,688
will you be able to use
the recreational facilities.

62
00:04:50,758 --> 00:04:52,769
Track and tennis
courts over here,

63
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:54,893
basketball court, swimming pool

64
00:04:54,962 --> 00:04:58,163
and putting greens on the
other side of the weight room.

65
00:04:58,232 --> 00:05:01,332
Beats the hell out of the state
pen, doesn't it, Chambers?

66
00:05:01,401 --> 00:05:05,937
No guard towers, no walls.

67
00:05:06,006 --> 00:05:08,439
Just a little fence.

68
00:05:08,508 --> 00:05:10,720
I don't have to tell you

69
00:05:10,744 --> 00:05:13,578
what'll happen if
you try to escape.

70
00:05:13,647 --> 00:05:17,515
Please, look... don't
ruin the moment.

71
00:05:17,584 --> 00:05:20,585
How'd you do it
anyway, Chambers?

72
00:05:20,654 --> 00:05:22,420
Do what?

73
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:24,255
This is where they send
creative bookkeepers

74
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:27,159
and inside traders,
corrupt politicians...

75
00:05:27,227 --> 00:05:29,227
You know, white collar crooks.

76
00:05:29,296 --> 00:05:30,962
What's a safecracker like you

77
00:05:31,031 --> 00:05:33,164
doing in a place like this?

78
00:05:33,233 --> 00:05:36,768
With any luck, about five years.

79
00:05:57,257 --> 00:05:58,423
What are you looking for?

80
00:05:58,492 --> 00:06:01,893
Anything that'll tell
me who killed Lenny.

81
00:06:01,962 --> 00:06:04,095
He killed himself.

82
00:06:04,164 --> 00:06:05,196
No.

83
00:06:05,265 --> 00:06:06,305
Lenny was a survivor.

84
00:06:06,366 --> 00:06:08,244
He knew he had
something that I wanted,

85
00:06:08,268 --> 00:06:10,835
and he knew I'd
make a deal to get it.

86
00:06:10,904 --> 00:06:12,749
I just didn't get
to him in time.

87
00:06:12,773 --> 00:06:13,983
He'd never have killed himself

88
00:06:14,007 --> 00:06:15,718
till he heard what
I had to offer.

89
00:06:15,742 --> 00:06:17,175
Well, then who killed him?

90
00:06:17,244 --> 00:06:21,813
Whoever killed Rudy.

91
00:06:21,882 --> 00:06:24,116
The first place to
look is under the bed.

92
00:06:39,666 --> 00:06:41,532
It's bloody.

93
00:06:41,601 --> 00:06:43,134
Yeah.

94
00:06:43,203 --> 00:06:46,070
And I'll bet anything it's
Rudy Chambers' blood.

95
00:06:46,139 --> 00:06:48,506
What's Lenny doing with it?

96
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:51,176
Well, either Lenny killed him...

97
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:53,077
The wimp?!

98
00:06:53,146 --> 00:06:57,415
Or he took the knife after
somebody else killed him.

99
00:06:57,484 --> 00:07:00,418
Lenny knew this knife
would implicate somebody,

100
00:07:00,487 --> 00:07:03,488
so he kept it, figuring
the killer wouldn't kill him.

101
00:07:03,557 --> 00:07:05,223
In other words, Tiny,

102
00:07:05,291 --> 00:07:07,959
if we can find out
who owns this knife,

103
00:07:08,028 --> 00:07:10,094
we'll know who the killer is.

104
00:07:14,034 --> 00:07:15,767
Damn.

105
00:07:15,836 --> 00:07:17,702
You recognize it?

106
00:07:17,771 --> 00:07:20,005
No.

107
00:07:24,844 --> 00:07:27,546
Uh, appreciate it, man.

108
00:07:31,485 --> 00:07:35,953
You won't catch
me talking about it.

109
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:43,228
If I had that much time,

110
00:07:43,297 --> 00:07:45,863
then I wouldn't
be doing all of this.

111
00:07:45,932 --> 00:07:47,732
Not me, man.

112
00:07:50,671 --> 00:07:52,737
Oh, just the boys
I was looking for.

113
00:07:52,806 --> 00:07:55,106
Man, when are you
going to get off our backs?

114
00:07:55,175 --> 00:07:58,876
Well, just as
soon as I figure out

115
00:07:58,945 --> 00:08:01,491
which one of you
killed Rudy Chambers

116
00:08:01,515 --> 00:08:02,947
and Lenny Marcus.

117
00:08:03,016 --> 00:08:05,450
Whoa-whoa, wait... now
one of us killed Lenny, too?

118
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:08,798
I know one of you killed Rudy.

119
00:08:08,822 --> 00:08:10,500
If he hadn't blown
the whistle on you,

120
00:08:10,524 --> 00:08:13,324
why you'd all be on the beach
in South America or somewhere.

121
00:08:13,393 --> 00:08:15,259
Hell, maybe you
were all in on it.

122
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:16,361
Drew straws or something.

123
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:18,310
Lenny was a friend of ours, Ben.

124
00:08:18,364 --> 00:08:20,232
Why would we want to kill him?

125
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:24,769
Because one of you bribed
Lenny to look the other way

126
00:08:24,838 --> 00:08:27,305
while Rudy was being killed.

127
00:08:27,373 --> 00:08:29,507
And that was okay then,

128
00:08:29,575 --> 00:08:33,144
but then this kangaroo
court thing came up

129
00:08:33,213 --> 00:08:36,614
and you were afraid
that somebody else

130
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:39,183
might bribe Lenny... me.

131
00:08:39,253 --> 00:08:42,153
And so, one of you,

132
00:08:42,222 --> 00:08:45,356
the one with the most to lose,

133
00:08:45,425 --> 00:08:48,226
the one who killed
Rudy, killed Lenny.

134
00:08:48,295 --> 00:08:50,461
Lenny hung himself.

135
00:08:50,531 --> 00:08:53,397
You know as well as I
do Lenny wasn't the type.

136
00:08:53,466 --> 00:08:55,866
If you're waiting for one
of us to confess here,

137
00:08:55,936 --> 00:08:57,468
don't hold your breath.

138
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:04,909
The reason I came to see you
is I've got something to tell you.

139
00:09:04,978 --> 00:09:06,410
What's that?

140
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:09,113
We found the murder
weapon in Lenny's cell.

141
00:09:10,551 --> 00:09:12,717
You found the knife?

142
00:09:12,786 --> 00:09:14,418
We found<i> a</i> knife.

143
00:09:14,487 --> 00:09:17,789
We found<i> a</i> knife.

144
00:09:17,858 --> 00:09:23,261
Now, the warden is
willing to make a deal

145
00:09:23,329 --> 00:09:28,199
with anybody who knows anything
about Rudy Chambers' murder.

146
00:09:28,268 --> 00:09:30,735
And I figure

147
00:09:30,804 --> 00:09:33,772
two of you might be interested.

148
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:35,340
Let me know.

149
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:37,775
I'm easy to find.

150
00:09:50,323 --> 00:09:52,022
What's wrong, man?

151
00:09:52,091 --> 00:09:54,236
I wasn't supposed to
tell them about the knife?

152
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:57,127
No, Tiny, you weren't supposed
to tell them about the knife.

153
00:09:57,196 --> 00:09:58,574
You didn't tell me that!

154
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:00,732
I didn't think I had to!

155
00:10:16,182 --> 00:10:17,915
Chambers?

156
00:10:17,984 --> 00:10:20,885
You're blocking my rays.

157
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:22,231
I'm Lesser.

158
00:10:22,255 --> 00:10:24,655
Nice to meet you.

159
00:10:27,494 --> 00:10:29,794
Could you move about
six inches to the right?

160
00:10:29,863 --> 00:10:32,396
I have a message from Harper.

161
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:34,298
I'm listening.

162
00:10:34,368 --> 00:10:38,069
Get acquainted
meeting tonight at 10:00.

163
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:39,904
312 Valley Vista.

164
00:10:39,973 --> 00:10:41,239
Enjoy.

165
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:46,711
I never seen it before.

166
00:10:46,779 --> 00:10:49,914
According to Tiny, nearly
everybody in this place

167
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:52,350
makes himself some
kind of a weapon.

168
00:10:52,418 --> 00:10:55,954
I thought maybe you might recognize the
way this tape's wrapped around the handle

169
00:10:56,022 --> 00:10:58,289
as being somebody's trademark.

170
00:10:58,358 --> 00:11:00,458
I don't know.

171
00:11:00,526 --> 00:11:02,604
Things are looking up, you know.

172
00:11:02,628 --> 00:11:05,496
We finally have something
that can implicate the real killer.

173
00:11:05,565 --> 00:11:07,965
A good solid piece of evidence.

174
00:11:08,034 --> 00:11:09,934
You don't get it, do you?

175
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:12,737
You keep talking like this
thing is for real, and it's not.

176
00:11:12,806 --> 00:11:14,205
It's a joke.

177
00:11:14,274 --> 00:11:15,840
The same thing
is going to happen,

178
00:11:15,909 --> 00:11:17,742
whether you find
the real killer or not.

179
00:11:17,811 --> 00:11:19,444
They're gonna kill<i> me.</i>

180
00:11:46,239 --> 00:11:48,172
♪ ♪

181
00:12:05,758 --> 00:12:06,791
<i>I'm Jim Beck.</i>

182
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:07,992
<i>This is Mike Saunders.</i>

183
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:10,528
How you doin'?

184
00:12:10,597 --> 00:12:12,797
I'm here.

185
00:12:12,866 --> 00:12:16,133
So... where's Harper?

186
00:12:16,202 --> 00:12:20,004
You probably won't
see him till after the job.

187
00:12:22,576 --> 00:12:23,576
When's the job?

188
00:12:23,643 --> 00:12:25,243
Tomorrow night.

189
00:12:25,311 --> 00:12:26,556
Had us worried.

190
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:29,013
Figured that prison riot
screwed everything up.

191
00:12:29,082 --> 00:12:31,916
Yeah, well, riot broke out

192
00:12:31,984 --> 00:12:35,119
just as I was being
transferred to Greenwood.

193
00:12:35,188 --> 00:12:36,265
Harper gave us your list.

194
00:12:36,289 --> 00:12:37,188
We got everything
you wanted in there.

195
00:12:37,257 --> 00:12:38,856
You mind if I look at it?

196
00:12:38,925 --> 00:12:41,191
Be my guest.

197
00:12:55,074 --> 00:12:56,874
Yeah...

198
00:12:56,943 --> 00:12:59,276
Yeah, that looks,
that looks good.

199
00:12:59,345 --> 00:13:04,214
That... looks like
it's, uh, it's all here.

200
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:07,117
That's nice work.

201
00:13:08,622 --> 00:13:13,891
So, guess I'll see you
boys tomorrow night.

202
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,259
And where you going?

203
00:13:15,328 --> 00:13:16,994
Out. No, no.

204
00:13:17,063 --> 00:13:18,674
You're an escaped con, remember?

205
00:13:18,698 --> 00:13:20,899
You're not going
anywhere till after the job.

206
00:13:22,469 --> 00:13:26,771
You need to get out here
and work out a little bit.

207
00:13:40,287 --> 00:13:42,553
So where's your new
homeboy... the lawyer?

208
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:48,737
Talking to Mazarofski, man.

209
00:13:48,761 --> 00:13:50,873
He told me to take a walk.

210
00:13:50,897 --> 00:13:51,830
Probably figures

211
00:13:51,898 --> 00:13:53,464
an uneducated guy like you

212
00:13:53,533 --> 00:13:58,136
would get lost with
all the legal talk.

213
00:13:58,205 --> 00:14:00,705
Or maybe he just
doesn't trust you.

214
00:14:00,773 --> 00:14:02,574
Listen, Tiny,

215
00:14:02,642 --> 00:14:05,876
I got this friend who'd like
to know more about that shiv

216
00:14:05,945 --> 00:14:07,378
you found in Lenny's cell.

217
00:14:07,447 --> 00:14:09,547
What's in it for me?

218
00:14:09,616 --> 00:14:11,115
Plenty.

219
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:12,783
What'd it look like?

220
00:14:12,853 --> 00:14:14,785
It's a mess hall knife, man.

221
00:14:14,855 --> 00:14:17,054
It's filed down,
black tape for a grip.

222
00:14:17,123 --> 00:14:19,624
Where's it now?

223
00:14:19,693 --> 00:14:21,359
It's locked in solitary.

224
00:14:21,428 --> 00:14:25,062
You think, if I gave you
the word ahead of time,

225
00:14:25,131 --> 00:14:28,132
you could leave that cell
unlocked for an hour or two?

226
00:14:30,537 --> 00:14:31,835
No problem.

227
00:14:59,165 --> 00:15:01,399
♪ ♪

228
00:15:38,137 --> 00:15:39,770
♪ ♪

229
00:15:55,521 --> 00:15:58,756
That's a security peep
from the bank lobby.

230
00:15:58,825 --> 00:16:01,158
We planted a transmitter
on one of the poles they use

231
00:16:01,227 --> 00:16:02,427
to rope off the teller area.

232
00:16:02,462 --> 00:16:03,628
Signals from this makes it

233
00:16:03,697 --> 00:16:05,730
vibrate just enough

234
00:16:05,799 --> 00:16:07,109
to set off the motion detector.

235
00:16:07,133 --> 00:16:08,411
We've been
triggering it a couple

236
00:16:08,435 --> 00:16:10,395
of times a night,
for almost a week.

237
00:16:10,437 --> 00:16:12,502
And here we go again.

238
00:16:20,846 --> 00:16:23,414
Motion on the main floor.

239
00:16:23,483 --> 00:16:26,317
Nothing's moving down there.

240
00:16:26,386 --> 00:16:28,386
I don't care what
Maintenance says.

241
00:16:28,454 --> 00:16:30,166
There's a short in the
system somewhere,

242
00:16:30,190 --> 00:16:31,200
damn it.

243
00:16:31,224 --> 00:16:32,590
It's your turn to check.

244
00:17:03,222 --> 00:17:05,122
Give him a couple of minutes

245
00:17:05,191 --> 00:17:07,111
to get back upstairs
to his buddy.

246
00:17:12,598 --> 00:17:13,809
A million bucks

247
00:17:13,833 --> 00:17:16,834
for a security system
that doesn't work.

248
00:17:16,903 --> 00:17:21,238
And now...

249
00:17:21,307 --> 00:17:22,406
it's showtime.

250
00:17:33,586 --> 00:17:35,052
You're feeding 'em the tape?

251
00:17:35,121 --> 00:17:36,420
Two hours of empty lobby.

252
00:17:36,489 --> 00:17:37,569
Recorded it last night.

253
00:17:38,858 --> 00:17:40,457
Ready when you are.

254
00:17:40,527 --> 00:17:41,959
Let's hit it.

255
00:17:50,102 --> 00:17:51,368
I say we pull the plug.

256
00:18:24,003 --> 00:18:25,269
Okay.

257
00:18:44,491 --> 00:18:47,158
It's all yours.

258
00:18:59,038 --> 00:19:02,039
Yeah, there we go.

259
00:19:02,108 --> 00:19:04,275
See what you got for me.

260
00:19:16,456 --> 00:19:17,722
It's thick.

261
00:19:28,401 --> 00:19:29,612
You're supposed to be fast.

262
00:19:29,636 --> 00:19:31,535
What's taking so long?

263
00:19:31,604 --> 00:19:32,981
Hey, I learned this
from Charlie Hawk.

264
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:34,383
He's the best
safecracker in the country.

265
00:19:34,407 --> 00:19:36,185
But if you think you
can get somebody faster,

266
00:19:36,209 --> 00:19:37,409
you're welcome to go get him.

267
00:20:00,266 --> 00:20:01,765
Come on, man!

268
00:20:01,834 --> 00:20:04,635
We got nine minutes
left on that video.

269
00:20:09,475 --> 00:20:10,674
Uh...

270
00:20:12,711 --> 00:20:13,811
I think that's it.

271
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:15,479
You<i> think?</i>

272
00:20:21,688 --> 00:20:23,832
Yeah, yeah.

273
00:20:23,856 --> 00:20:24,936
Come on.

274
00:20:36,268 --> 00:20:37,535
Yes!

275
00:20:37,603 --> 00:20:39,970
How much you
figure, one, two million?

276
00:20:40,039 --> 00:20:42,673
Who's counting?

277
00:20:45,712 --> 00:20:46,922
Who wants a beer?

278
00:20:46,946 --> 00:20:48,078
Make it two.

279
00:20:48,848 --> 00:20:49,925
Rudy!

280
00:20:49,949 --> 00:20:51,360
See, now, ordinarily, I'd pass,

281
00:20:51,384 --> 00:20:53,562
but, right now, I'm, I'm
feeling congenial, guys.

282
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:55,466
A good day at the office.

283
00:20:57,257 --> 00:20:59,090
There's two million at least.

284
00:20:59,158 --> 00:21:01,791
I was starting to get worried.

285
00:21:01,861 --> 00:21:04,361
Chambers here was
a little out of practice.

286
00:21:07,667 --> 00:21:09,233
That's not Chambers.

287
00:21:13,673 --> 00:21:15,072
Who are you?

288
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,468
Travis Jenkins.

289
00:21:32,492 --> 00:21:35,058
Yes, and I've been in
the pen for five years,

290
00:21:35,127 --> 00:21:36,894
and Rudy's one
of my best buddies.

291
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:38,829
What, he ne... he
never said anything

292
00:21:38,898 --> 00:21:40,197
to you about me?

293
00:21:40,266 --> 00:21:42,210
What happened to Rudy
Chambers, Mr. Jenkins?

294
00:21:42,234 --> 00:21:44,368
He busted his arm
breaking out, I told you.

295
00:21:44,437 --> 00:21:47,238
He couldn't crack a
paper bag, let alone a vault.

296
00:21:47,307 --> 00:21:49,373
Which is why he
told me about the plan

297
00:21:49,442 --> 00:21:51,074
and had me fill in for him.

298
00:21:51,144 --> 00:21:52,221
Bull! It's true!

299
00:21:52,245 --> 00:21:54,177
Half of my take's
gonna be waiting for him

300
00:21:54,247 --> 00:21:55,512
when he gets out.

301
00:21:55,581 --> 00:21:58,249
He told me because he...
Look, half of something

302
00:21:58,317 --> 00:22:01,351
is better than all of
nothing, am I right?

303
00:22:01,421 --> 00:22:03,888
How come you didn't tell
us all this right from the start?

304
00:22:03,956 --> 00:22:05,400
Because I figured you
wouldn't let me pull the job.

305
00:22:05,424 --> 00:22:06,868
You were right. See?!

306
00:22:06,892 --> 00:22:08,671
But I pulled through, didn't I?

307
00:22:08,695 --> 00:22:11,729
I'm gonna check...

308
00:22:11,798 --> 00:22:14,198
see if Travis Jenkins
really was a prisoner

309
00:22:14,266 --> 00:22:15,799
in the pen for five years.

310
00:22:21,007 --> 00:22:22,117
Without mentioning specifics,

311
00:22:22,141 --> 00:22:23,952
authorities here at
the Atlanta State Prison

312
00:22:23,976 --> 00:22:26,310
say they are making
progress in their negotiations

313
00:22:26,378 --> 00:22:29,546
with the inmates who are
now in control of the facility.

314
00:22:29,615 --> 00:22:32,916
They refused to comment
on the trial going on inside.

315
00:22:32,985 --> 00:22:36,553
Mr. Stone, would you
please tell the court

316
00:22:36,622 --> 00:22:40,057
what it was you saw
on the night of the 21st?

317
00:22:40,126 --> 00:22:41,725
Well, Mr. Mazarofski,
uh, you know,

318
00:22:41,793 --> 00:22:45,162
I hurt my knee while I
was working in the laundry.

319
00:22:45,231 --> 00:22:47,331
A, uh, press door
fell over, whacked me

320
00:22:47,399 --> 00:22:48,499
right across the kneecap.

321
00:22:48,567 --> 00:22:50,468
Hurt so bad, I didn't
know what to do.

322
00:22:50,536 --> 00:22:51,669
Why don't you sue?!

323
00:22:51,737 --> 00:22:54,638
Shut up before I come
over and sue you, man!

324
00:22:54,707 --> 00:22:56,018
All right!

325
00:22:56,042 --> 00:22:57,941
You don't know who
you messing with!

326
00:23:00,813 --> 00:23:05,149
Order! Order or
I'll clear this room.

327
00:23:05,218 --> 00:23:08,385
That means pipe down or get out.

328
00:23:09,721 --> 00:23:12,189
Yeah, yeah.

329
00:23:12,258 --> 00:23:14,491
All right, so you
hurt your kneecap

330
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:16,038
and you went to the infirmary

331
00:23:16,062 --> 00:23:17,561
to get it fixed up, right?

332
00:23:17,630 --> 00:23:19,863
Yeah, yeah, that's right.

333
00:23:21,867 --> 00:23:23,934
What did you see?

334
00:23:24,003 --> 00:23:27,637
Well, first, I saw
John Jackson standing

335
00:23:27,706 --> 00:23:29,306
above one of the beds.

336
00:23:29,375 --> 00:23:34,945
Then I saw Rudy Chambers<i>
laying</i> on one of the beds.

337
00:23:35,014 --> 00:23:37,614
And the minute I saw the
brother, I knew he was dead.

338
00:23:37,683 --> 00:23:38,883
He had been wasted,

339
00:23:38,951 --> 00:23:40,629
'cause there was
blood all over the place.

340
00:23:40,653 --> 00:23:43,153
Did you see anyone else?

341
00:23:43,222 --> 00:23:46,757
Just Jackson.

342
00:23:46,826 --> 00:23:49,059
That's it...!

343
00:23:49,128 --> 00:23:52,029
Hang him, Judge!

344
00:23:52,098 --> 00:23:53,396
No further questions.

345
00:23:54,199 --> 00:23:59,870
Ah, uh, Mr. Stone...

346
00:23:59,939 --> 00:24:03,874
did you actually
see the defendant,

347
00:24:03,943 --> 00:24:08,345
John Jackson, stab
Rudy Chambers?

348
00:24:08,414 --> 00:24:09,613
Yeah, I saw him...

349
00:24:09,682 --> 00:24:10,580
You're a damn liar, Stone!

350
00:24:10,650 --> 00:24:12,382
Hey, man, don't call me no liar!

351
00:24:13,453 --> 00:24:15,786
Order!

352
00:24:17,557 --> 00:24:22,426
You do that again, I'll have you
bound and gagged, Mr. Jackson.

353
00:24:27,033 --> 00:24:29,599
Now, let me ask you again.

354
00:24:29,668 --> 00:24:33,504
Did you actually
see the defendant,

355
00:24:33,572 --> 00:24:36,740
John Jackson, stab
Rudy Chambers?

356
00:24:36,809 --> 00:24:39,076
He was standing right over him.

357
00:24:39,145 --> 00:24:41,845
Did you see him
holding the knife?

358
00:24:43,615 --> 00:24:46,450
Let me... Well, now, I
didn't actually see the knife,

359
00:24:46,519 --> 00:24:47,684
you understand?

360
00:24:47,753 --> 00:24:49,913
Oh, oh, so you didn't
actually see the murder,

361
00:24:49,955 --> 00:24:51,600
and you didn't
actually see the knife.

362
00:24:51,624 --> 00:24:54,124
You didn't see much of
anything, did you, Mr. Stone?

363
00:24:54,192 --> 00:24:55,804
You saw the knife!
Nothing further.

364
00:24:55,828 --> 00:24:57,172
Hey, wait, hey...
Witness is excused.

365
00:24:57,196 --> 00:24:58,540
Hey, you!

366
00:24:58,564 --> 00:25:01,197
I saw John Jackson

367
00:25:01,267 --> 00:25:04,334
standing over Rudy
Chambers' dead, bleeding body.

368
00:25:04,403 --> 00:25:05,835
That's what I saw, man!

369
00:25:05,905 --> 00:25:07,103
Aw, shut up and get down.

370
00:25:07,173 --> 00:25:08,517
I'm trying to explain the...

371
00:25:08,541 --> 00:25:09,606
Time for dinner.

372
00:25:09,675 --> 00:25:11,320
This court's
adjourned till 9:00 or so

373
00:25:11,344 --> 00:25:12,344
tomorrow morning.

374
00:25:25,358 --> 00:25:26,638
Say, Tiny...

375
00:25:28,794 --> 00:25:32,596
have that cell open
by 10:00 tonight, okay?

376
00:25:32,665 --> 00:25:34,598
Okay.

377
00:25:53,319 --> 00:25:55,652
What's going on, Art?

378
00:25:55,721 --> 00:25:57,654
Stay back, both of you.

379
00:26:02,194 --> 00:26:04,094
Whose side are you on, Tiny?

380
00:26:04,162 --> 00:26:06,763
Rudy Chambers
was a friend of mine.

381
00:26:09,167 --> 00:26:10,634
I didn't kill him.

382
00:26:10,703 --> 00:26:13,770
But he was the reason
your escape failed.

383
00:26:13,839 --> 00:26:15,105
He snitched on you.

384
00:26:15,173 --> 00:26:18,308
As I understand it, around
here, that's a capital crime.

385
00:26:18,377 --> 00:26:19,876
I didn't kill him.

386
00:26:19,946 --> 00:26:22,145
What are you in for, Mr. Spring?

387
00:26:22,214 --> 00:26:24,981
Murder one, two counts.

388
00:26:25,051 --> 00:26:26,816
Oh, an experienced killer.

389
00:26:26,886 --> 00:26:28,385
But I didn't kill Rudy Chambers.

390
00:26:30,489 --> 00:26:34,157
This knife is the murder weapon.

391
00:26:34,226 --> 00:26:38,796
Tiny and I found
it in Lenny's cell.

392
00:26:38,864 --> 00:26:40,542
My guess is that he took it

393
00:26:40,566 --> 00:26:43,111
out of Rudy Chamber"
body as insurance.

394
00:26:43,135 --> 00:26:47,370
If he had the knife, he'd
be safe from the killer.

395
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:48,771
Whose knife is it,

396
00:26:48,841 --> 00:26:49,773
Mr. Spring?

397
00:26:49,842 --> 00:26:51,241
It's mine. But I'm...

398
00:26:51,310 --> 00:26:54,945
You killed Rudy Chambers
and then you killed Lenny Marcus

399
00:26:55,014 --> 00:26:57,492
because you were afraid he was
gonna squeal on you, didn't you?

400
00:26:57,516 --> 00:26:58,748
No!

401
00:26:58,818 --> 00:27:01,351
Then why was your
knife in Lenny's cell?!

402
00:27:01,420 --> 00:27:05,255
Somebody stole it from me
and used it on Rudy Chambers

403
00:27:05,324 --> 00:27:07,257
to frame me for the murder!

404
00:27:07,326 --> 00:27:08,758
Oh, come on!

405
00:27:08,828 --> 00:27:10,327
If I was the killer,

406
00:27:10,395 --> 00:27:12,474
I would've torn Lenny's cell
apart looking for that knife.

407
00:27:12,498 --> 00:27:16,933
You found it because whoever
did kill Rudy wanted you to.

408
00:27:17,003 --> 00:27:20,371
Because it wasn't
his knife, it was mine!

409
00:27:21,540 --> 00:27:23,840
All right.

410
00:27:23,909 --> 00:27:27,277
Where were you at
the time of the murder?

411
00:27:27,346 --> 00:27:31,648
I was right here,
watching the Braves game.

412
00:27:34,754 --> 00:27:36,553
Anybody watching it with you?

413
00:27:36,622 --> 00:27:37,554
Of course.

414
00:27:37,623 --> 00:27:38,721
Lots of guys.

415
00:27:38,791 --> 00:27:39,889
Who?

416
00:27:39,959 --> 00:27:41,570
I don't know! I don't remember!

417
00:27:41,594 --> 00:27:45,228
Nobody was watching
that game that night,

418
00:27:45,297 --> 00:27:47,008
not even you, Mr. Spring,

419
00:27:47,032 --> 00:27:49,733
because it wasn't on.

420
00:27:49,802 --> 00:27:53,403
Here's the TV station's
daily broadcast log.

421
00:27:53,472 --> 00:27:55,973
Read me what it says
about the Braves game.

422
00:28:01,780 --> 00:28:03,680
Okay, so the game wasn't on.

423
00:28:03,748 --> 00:28:05,749
I must have been
watching it some other night.

424
00:28:08,386 --> 00:28:12,990
Again, where were you
at the time of the murder?

425
00:28:13,059 --> 00:28:15,892
I don't remember.

426
00:28:15,961 --> 00:28:18,529
Hell, I bet half the guys in
this room can't remember

427
00:28:18,597 --> 00:28:20,163
what they were
doing that night either!

428
00:28:23,102 --> 00:28:26,103
The knife that killed
Rudy Chambers

429
00:28:26,171 --> 00:28:28,972
doesn't belong to any
of them, it belongs to you.

430
00:28:29,041 --> 00:28:29,973
That's right!

431
00:28:30,042 --> 00:28:32,442
All right.

432
00:28:32,511 --> 00:28:34,912
I'll tell you.

433
00:28:34,980 --> 00:28:36,479
But just remember, Matlock,

434
00:28:36,549 --> 00:28:39,316
if anything happens
to me, it's on your head.

435
00:28:39,385 --> 00:28:41,451
Now you remember where you were.

436
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:45,455
I was talking to Frank Latham.

437
00:28:47,226 --> 00:28:48,492
Who's Frank Latham?

438
00:28:48,561 --> 00:28:50,627
He's one of the guards.

439
00:28:52,732 --> 00:28:53,997
You're a snitch?

440
00:29:04,176 --> 00:29:05,408
If you kill this man,

441
00:29:05,477 --> 00:29:07,577
you're gonna destroy
everything we've done so far.

442
00:29:07,646 --> 00:29:08,578
Back off.

443
00:29:08,647 --> 00:29:09,579
Move it, man!

444
00:29:09,648 --> 00:29:11,347
Look, they're
negotiating with us.

445
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:15,018
We can get our demands,
if you just don't blow it.

446
00:29:15,087 --> 00:29:16,932
We can't continue
with this trial if you don't

447
00:29:16,956 --> 00:29:20,891
turn this man over to the
authorities, outside, alive!

448
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:25,763
Shut up!

449
00:29:25,831 --> 00:29:26,831
Shut up!

450
00:29:27,833 --> 00:29:29,199
To hell with Spring!

451
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:31,000
Let the warden have him!

452
00:29:31,069 --> 00:29:33,269
Once a snitch, always a snitch.

453
00:29:33,339 --> 00:29:34,849
Let him have him dead!

454
00:29:34,873 --> 00:29:36,740
He'll get what he's
got coming to him.

455
00:29:36,809 --> 00:29:37,809
Tiny.

456
00:29:37,877 --> 00:29:40,877
Take Mr. Spring to the gate.

457
00:29:40,946 --> 00:29:43,213
If anybody asks,

458
00:29:43,282 --> 00:29:45,248
tell them you're
dumping the trash.

459
00:29:56,061 --> 00:29:57,271
All right.

460
00:29:57,295 --> 00:29:59,007
Get back in your seats.

461
00:29:59,031 --> 00:30:01,298
Everybody, sit down!

462
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:06,614
And to add insult to injury,

463
00:30:06,638 --> 00:30:08,349
he threw it over
Randolph's head,

464
00:30:08,373 --> 00:30:10,807
allowing Harmon to
score from second base.

465
00:30:10,876 --> 00:30:13,409
In the seventh inning
though, it was all Braves.

466
00:30:13,479 --> 00:30:14,945
Aaron led off with a smash...

467
00:30:15,013 --> 00:30:16,980
Hey, why don't you turn it up.

468
00:30:20,553 --> 00:30:23,186
Where do you think you're going?

469
00:30:23,255 --> 00:30:25,722
I'm thirsty.

470
00:30:25,791 --> 00:30:28,358
Go ahead.

471
00:31:54,179 --> 00:31:55,912
All right, you in the van,

472
00:31:55,981 --> 00:31:58,681
you in the car, come out with
your hands above your head!

473
00:32:00,619 --> 00:32:03,131
Everybody up against the van!

474
00:32:03,155 --> 00:32:05,455
Put your hands behind your head.

475
00:32:05,524 --> 00:32:07,257
Move it!

476
00:32:07,325 --> 00:32:08,485
Feet apart.

477
00:32:26,945 --> 00:32:30,413
Yet another National Guard
unit has just arrived on the scene.

478
00:32:30,482 --> 00:32:33,950
While prison officials are still
not giving out any information,

479
00:32:34,019 --> 00:32:35,830
it's clear from the
kind of firepower

480
00:32:35,854 --> 00:32:37,888
being amassed
outside these gates

481
00:32:37,956 --> 00:32:40,423
that some sort of assault
on the prison is imminent.

482
00:32:40,492 --> 00:32:44,194
Burt, you can't do that!

483
00:32:44,262 --> 00:32:47,330
I know what you said,
but you're the governor.

484
00:32:47,399 --> 00:32:50,300
Tell them you changed your mind.

485
00:32:50,369 --> 00:32:53,936
Burt, I told you,
they won't let me go.

486
00:32:54,006 --> 00:32:55,816
Of course I'm making progress.

487
00:32:55,840 --> 00:32:58,641
I need 48 hours.

488
00:32:58,711 --> 00:33:00,443
All right.

489
00:33:00,512 --> 00:33:03,146
All right, I'll
talk to you then.

490
00:33:03,215 --> 00:33:05,648
Hey, Burt...

491
00:33:05,718 --> 00:33:07,350
I didn't vote for you.

492
00:33:08,821 --> 00:33:10,186
He gave you two more days?

493
00:33:10,255 --> 00:33:12,233
He wants me out
of here in six hours.

494
00:33:12,257 --> 00:33:14,958
When this is over,
let's impeach him.

495
00:33:16,294 --> 00:33:17,304
Ben...

496
00:33:17,328 --> 00:33:18,406
Yeah.

497
00:33:18,430 --> 00:33:20,008
Oh, I hope you have
some good news.

498
00:33:20,032 --> 00:33:22,232
Good news... I got great news.

499
00:33:22,301 --> 00:33:25,101
Now, Mr. Costello...

500
00:33:27,072 --> 00:33:29,105
Uh...

501
00:33:29,174 --> 00:33:31,285
wh-what are you in for?

502
00:33:31,309 --> 00:33:33,009
Robbing a couple jewelry stores.

503
00:33:33,078 --> 00:33:35,011
That's what they say I did.

504
00:33:35,080 --> 00:33:36,646
I'm innocent, of course.

505
00:33:44,089 --> 00:33:45,321
Yeah, yeah.

506
00:33:45,390 --> 00:33:49,759
Now, uh, these, uh,
these, uh, robberies...

507
00:33:49,828 --> 00:33:51,573
Alleged robberies...
That, uh, that you pulled...

508
00:33:51,597 --> 00:33:53,195
Did you work alone?

509
00:33:53,265 --> 00:33:55,505
They say I had partners.
Never caught 'em, though.

510
00:33:55,567 --> 00:33:57,867
Oh, they couldn't get
you to rat on 'em, huh?

511
00:33:59,338 --> 00:34:00,270
A man of principle.

512
00:34:00,339 --> 00:34:03,840
Well, uh... what,
what was your, uh,

513
00:34:03,908 --> 00:34:07,477
what was your job in
these alleged robberies?

514
00:34:07,546 --> 00:34:08,945
Plastics.

515
00:34:09,014 --> 00:34:10,179
As in explosives.

516
00:34:10,249 --> 00:34:11,881
Uh-huh.

517
00:34:11,950 --> 00:34:16,085
Uh, do you suppose
your alleged friends

518
00:34:16,154 --> 00:34:20,990
could pull off one of these
robberies without you?

519
00:34:21,060 --> 00:34:23,060
Be pretty tough.

520
00:34:23,128 --> 00:34:24,972
Always gotta blow a
hole in something...

521
00:34:24,996 --> 00:34:28,899
Door, wall... safe.

522
00:34:28,967 --> 00:34:31,067
Plastics work best.

523
00:34:31,135 --> 00:34:32,769
On-On vaults, too?

524
00:34:32,838 --> 00:34:34,904
Vaults are a different story.

525
00:34:34,973 --> 00:34:36,818
Pretty tough to
blow a hole in a vault

526
00:34:36,842 --> 00:34:38,453
without attracting
a lot of attention.

527
00:34:38,477 --> 00:34:40,276
Or so I've heard.

528
00:34:40,345 --> 00:34:41,911
Uh-huh.

529
00:34:41,980 --> 00:34:46,449
So-So, i-i-if you were
gonna, say, oh, rob a place,

530
00:34:46,518 --> 00:34:49,151
and had to deal with a vault,

531
00:34:49,220 --> 00:34:52,288
then, uh, then-then
you'd have to employ

532
00:34:52,357 --> 00:34:53,823
the aid of a safecracker,

533
00:34:53,892 --> 00:34:55,737
wouldn't you? That's right.

534
00:34:55,761 --> 00:34:58,161
And Rudy Chambers was
a safecracker, wasn't he?

535
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:02,765
Now, let's say that, uh,

536
00:35:02,834 --> 00:35:05,368
let's say that your
friends on the outside...

537
00:35:05,437 --> 00:35:08,771
Yeah, here... let's say
that their names are, are

538
00:35:08,840 --> 00:35:12,842
Ed Harper, uh, Jim
Beck and Mike Sanders.

539
00:35:12,911 --> 00:35:15,678
Is that all right?

540
00:35:15,747 --> 00:35:16,679
Uh-huh.

541
00:35:16,748 --> 00:35:18,180
And let's say that, uh,

542
00:35:18,250 --> 00:35:21,150
let's say that, uh, they
decide they want to rob a bank,

543
00:35:21,220 --> 00:35:24,387
and so, somehow,
they got word to you.

544
00:35:24,456 --> 00:35:27,824
And the plan was that you
would escape from prison here,

545
00:35:27,892 --> 00:35:31,761
just in time to help
them out with the heist.

546
00:35:31,830 --> 00:35:35,732
Only somewhere along the line...

547
00:35:35,801 --> 00:35:39,569
they realized they
had to deal with a vault.

548
00:35:39,638 --> 00:35:43,973
So they got you to
recruit Rudy Chambers.

549
00:35:44,042 --> 00:35:45,575
Right?

550
00:35:45,644 --> 00:35:47,944
I don't know what
you're talking about.

551
00:35:49,882 --> 00:35:51,781
The way I see it,

552
00:35:51,850 --> 00:35:54,618
the plan was...

553
00:35:54,686 --> 00:35:56,620
for you to escape.

554
00:35:56,688 --> 00:36:01,290
So you and Rudy got together
with Art Spring and Val Delaney,

555
00:36:01,359 --> 00:36:02,992
and planned this breakout.

556
00:36:03,061 --> 00:36:06,541
Of course, Art and Val didn't
know anything about the robbery.

557
00:36:06,565 --> 00:36:09,365
They just wanted to
get away from this place.

558
00:36:09,434 --> 00:36:10,711
Does that sound familiar?

559
00:36:12,203 --> 00:36:14,337
Not at all.

560
00:36:14,406 --> 00:36:17,374
Now, let's say your
friends got greedy.

561
00:36:17,442 --> 00:36:19,509
They got greedy.

562
00:36:19,577 --> 00:36:22,879
They realized they
didn't need you.

563
00:36:24,149 --> 00:36:27,217
But because of the
vault, they needed Rudy.

564
00:36:27,286 --> 00:36:30,320
So, they came up
with an ingenious plan

565
00:36:30,389 --> 00:36:32,855
to cut you out.

566
00:36:32,925 --> 00:36:35,658
The escape was going
along fine, going along fine,

567
00:36:35,727 --> 00:36:37,794
moving right along,
and all of a sudden...

568
00:36:39,064 --> 00:36:41,831
Rudy faked an injury.

569
00:36:41,900 --> 00:36:45,635
And the reason he did
that was to buy a transfer

570
00:36:45,703 --> 00:36:48,939
to Greenwood Prison
Camp... Easy to get out of,

571
00:36:49,007 --> 00:36:53,542
by informing on
you and your friends.

572
00:36:53,612 --> 00:36:56,446
You're making this
up as you go along.

573
00:36:56,515 --> 00:36:58,180
You know I'm not.

574
00:36:58,249 --> 00:36:59,516
You know I'm not!

575
00:37:00,986 --> 00:37:03,546
And now comes Lenny Marcus.

576
00:37:04,289 --> 00:37:07,090
When you found out

577
00:37:07,158 --> 00:37:09,959
that he snitched on Rudy,

578
00:37:10,028 --> 00:37:11,761
you decided... you knew...

579
00:37:11,830 --> 00:37:13,908
You knew that you'd
been double-crossed,

580
00:37:13,932 --> 00:37:16,044
and you decided you'd get even.

581
00:37:16,068 --> 00:37:18,201
And you killed the man

582
00:37:18,270 --> 00:37:21,538
that your friends needed
to get into that vault.

583
00:37:21,607 --> 00:37:23,606
You killed Rudy Chambers.

584
00:37:23,675 --> 00:37:25,320
Objection!

585
00:37:25,344 --> 00:37:29,379
Mr. Matlock is engaging
in rampant speculation.

586
00:37:29,448 --> 00:37:31,047
There's not a shred of proof.

587
00:37:31,116 --> 00:37:34,083
Your Honor, if you'll bear
with me, I do have proof.

588
00:37:34,152 --> 00:37:36,519
Go ahead.

589
00:37:36,588 --> 00:37:38,121
Thank you.

590
00:37:38,190 --> 00:37:40,756
Now, this is today's paper.

591
00:37:40,825 --> 00:37:43,393
You see here?

592
00:37:43,462 --> 00:37:46,562
Those men did
get into that vault.

593
00:37:46,632 --> 00:37:48,999
See?

594
00:37:49,067 --> 00:37:50,277
You see that?

595
00:37:50,301 --> 00:37:53,970
They got into the
vault. See that?

596
00:37:54,039 --> 00:37:56,305
See here?

597
00:37:56,374 --> 00:37:59,075
They got into the vault

598
00:37:59,144 --> 00:38:03,113
by using somebody they
thought was Rudy Chambers.

599
00:38:03,181 --> 00:38:04,481
Are you surprised?

600
00:38:06,551 --> 00:38:11,054
And guess whose van
they used for the getaway.

601
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:13,589
Yours.

602
00:38:15,126 --> 00:38:17,471
The police recovered it
when they arrested everybody.

603
00:38:17,495 --> 00:38:19,696
See? It says right here.

604
00:38:19,764 --> 00:38:23,332
"Police... Police
seized a vehicle

605
00:38:23,401 --> 00:38:27,336
"containing equipment
used in the bank robbery.

606
00:38:27,406 --> 00:38:31,140
"It was registered
to Billy Costello,

607
00:38:31,209 --> 00:38:34,411
currently an inmate at
Atlanta State Prison."

608
00:38:34,479 --> 00:38:35,999
See? They even
spelled your name right.

609
00:38:37,549 --> 00:38:38,815
I didn't kill Chambers.

610
00:38:38,884 --> 00:38:41,351
I was nowhere near him.
I was taking a shower.

611
00:38:41,419 --> 00:38:44,087
What?!

612
00:38:44,155 --> 00:38:45,755
When?!

613
00:38:45,824 --> 00:38:49,392
7:30 Wednesdays.

614
00:38:49,461 --> 00:38:51,727
After dinner, Cell Block
A always takes showers.

615
00:38:51,797 --> 00:38:53,195
Where?!

616
00:38:53,265 --> 00:38:55,131
On the cell block. Where else?

617
00:38:56,367 --> 00:39:00,036
So, on-on Wednesday...

618
00:39:00,105 --> 00:39:03,706
the day of the
murder, at 7:30...

619
00:39:03,775 --> 00:39:07,544
you were taking a
shower in Cell Block A.

620
00:39:07,612 --> 00:39:09,779
That's right.

621
00:39:09,848 --> 00:39:12,381
How'd your feet feel
after you got out?

622
00:39:14,786 --> 00:39:16,185
How'd my feet feel?

623
00:39:16,254 --> 00:39:19,055
Yeah.

624
00:39:19,124 --> 00:39:21,490
When I think I'm onto something,

625
00:39:21,559 --> 00:39:23,226
I don't miss a trick.

626
00:39:25,063 --> 00:39:27,363
Let's see here. Willie...

627
00:39:27,431 --> 00:39:29,565
Willie...

628
00:39:29,634 --> 00:39:30,745
yeah, Willie Lamberthal.

629
00:39:30,769 --> 00:39:34,070
Willie Lamberthal.

630
00:39:34,139 --> 00:39:37,840
He's the one that cleans
the, uh, the showers.

631
00:39:37,909 --> 00:39:41,577
Willie is ready to testify
that he had forgotten

632
00:39:41,646 --> 00:39:44,046
that-that Wednesday.

633
00:39:44,115 --> 00:39:46,582
And he put a big sign
on the shower door,

634
00:39:46,651 --> 00:39:48,885
said "Do not enter."

635
00:39:48,953 --> 00:39:52,588
And then about ten,
15, 20 minutes after 7:00,

636
00:39:52,657 --> 00:39:55,391
he poured a bunch of
this stuff on the floor.

637
00:39:55,459 --> 00:39:56,826
You know what it is?

638
00:39:56,895 --> 00:39:58,961
Disinfectant. That's right.

639
00:39:59,030 --> 00:40:02,131
Very powerful. Heavy duty.

640
00:40:02,199 --> 00:40:04,333
Mostly hydrochloric acid.

641
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:05,635
See that right there?

642
00:40:05,703 --> 00:40:08,638
It says "Danger. Contact
with the eyes or skin

643
00:40:08,706 --> 00:40:12,041
can cause serious injury."

644
00:40:12,110 --> 00:40:16,813
Willie tells me that
he leaves this stuff on

645
00:40:16,881 --> 00:40:20,984
from 15 to 25 minutes
to get it real clean, see?

646
00:40:21,052 --> 00:40:22,452
Then he washes it off.

647
00:40:23,788 --> 00:40:26,556
So, Mr. Costello, if
you took a shower

648
00:40:26,624 --> 00:40:28,558
that Wednesday at 7:30,

649
00:40:28,626 --> 00:40:29,759
you wouldn't be walking.

650
00:40:29,828 --> 00:40:32,328
Willie's lying.

651
00:40:32,396 --> 00:40:34,763
John Jackson paid him to lie.

652
00:40:34,833 --> 00:40:36,999
I don't think so!

653
00:40:37,068 --> 00:40:39,368
I don't think so!

654
00:40:39,437 --> 00:40:41,470
I don't think so!

655
00:40:41,539 --> 00:40:44,106
But I think<i> you...</i>

656
00:40:44,175 --> 00:40:47,009
paid Lenny to look the other way

657
00:40:47,078 --> 00:40:49,979
while you hit John Jackson
in the back of the head

658
00:40:50,048 --> 00:40:53,116
and drug him in the infirmary,
and then killed Rudy Chambers.

659
00:40:53,185 --> 00:40:55,051
It's a lie.

660
00:40:55,120 --> 00:40:57,920
It might've worked if it
hadn't been for this trial.

661
00:40:59,924 --> 00:41:03,159
But I got ahold of Lenny,

662
00:41:03,228 --> 00:41:06,862
and you knew I
wanted Lenny to talk.

663
00:41:06,931 --> 00:41:10,800
And you knew that
Lenny might break.

664
00:41:10,869 --> 00:41:13,802
So you killed Lenny.

665
00:41:15,606 --> 00:41:19,208
And then you tried
to frame Art Spring

666
00:41:19,277 --> 00:41:22,144
by planting his
shiv in Lenny's cell.

667
00:41:22,214 --> 00:41:24,446
No. Not a word of that is true.

668
00:41:24,516 --> 00:41:26,883
You promised Lenny

669
00:41:26,951 --> 00:41:30,486
that you would take care
of his cellmate, and you did.

670
00:41:30,555 --> 00:41:33,188
You promised
Lenny a lot of money.

671
00:41:33,257 --> 00:41:35,203
You promised him
it'd be waiting for him

672
00:41:35,227 --> 00:41:37,060
when he got out. Did not.

673
00:41:37,128 --> 00:41:38,828
All right.

674
00:41:38,896 --> 00:41:41,196
All right, explain this.

675
00:41:41,265 --> 00:41:44,566
Explain this, Mr. Costello.

676
00:41:44,636 --> 00:41:46,836
These are... are
bank statements.

677
00:41:46,905 --> 00:41:48,905
One is yours.

678
00:41:48,973 --> 00:41:51,741
One is Lenny's.

679
00:41:51,810 --> 00:41:55,211
On the day of the murder,

680
00:41:55,280 --> 00:42:00,183
your wife withdrew
$47,000 exactly

681
00:42:00,251 --> 00:42:06,422
from your savings
account, and, that same day,

682
00:42:06,491 --> 00:42:09,058
$47,000 appeared

683
00:42:09,126 --> 00:42:11,205
in Lenny's savings account.

684
00:42:11,229 --> 00:42:12,795
How do you explain that?

685
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:25,508
You paid... Lenny
Marcus... $47,000...

686
00:42:25,577 --> 00:42:29,178
to help set up and then cover up

687
00:42:29,247 --> 00:42:32,314
your murder of Rudy Chambers.

688
00:42:34,252 --> 00:42:37,820
That's all.

689
00:42:44,529 --> 00:42:46,941
About time!

690
00:42:46,965 --> 00:42:49,005
Let's get it straight this time.

691
00:42:49,968 --> 00:42:51,934
All right. Let's quiet down.

692
00:42:52,003 --> 00:42:55,738
C.J., did you
arrive at a verdict?

693
00:42:55,807 --> 00:42:57,874
We wouldn't be here
if we hadn't, Norman.

694
00:42:57,942 --> 00:42:59,942
Well, let's hear it.

695
00:43:00,011 --> 00:43:03,312
We didn't have a choice.

696
00:43:03,381 --> 00:43:06,983
We had to find John
Jackson not guilty.

697
00:43:10,455 --> 00:43:12,821
Wait, wait, wait.

698
00:43:16,093 --> 00:43:17,260
Wait!

699
00:43:17,329 --> 00:43:20,463
Now, we promised if he
was declared not guilty,

700
00:43:20,532 --> 00:43:21,764
we'd release him.

701
00:43:21,833 --> 00:43:22,932
So we lied!

702
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:24,244
Yeah, we lied!

703
00:43:24,268 --> 00:43:25,501
They lie to us all the time.

704
00:43:25,570 --> 00:43:27,181
If you kill this man,
they'll swarm this place

705
00:43:27,205 --> 00:43:28,416
like World War III.

706
00:43:28,440 --> 00:43:30,350
Half of you will be
killed and the rest of you

707
00:43:30,374 --> 00:43:32,119
will stay in here for
the rest of your lives.

708
00:43:32,143 --> 00:43:33,353
Is that what you want?

709
00:43:33,377 --> 00:43:34,655
You gave your word!

710
00:43:34,679 --> 00:43:36,657
Ah, save your breath. Shut up!

711
00:43:36,681 --> 00:43:38,914
Look, look... for once,
we got the upper hand.

712
00:43:38,984 --> 00:43:41,150
Now, I hate that guy's guts
just as much as anybody,

713
00:43:41,219 --> 00:43:44,320
but if we don't let him go,
they won't meet our demands.

714
00:43:45,991 --> 00:43:47,490
So what's up, man?

715
00:43:47,559 --> 00:43:50,192
All right, we're going to
listen to this bull this time.

716
00:43:51,930 --> 00:43:53,607
But you better
have it right, though.

717
00:43:53,631 --> 00:43:54,842
Better have it right.

718
00:43:54,866 --> 00:43:55,943
Yeah!

719
00:43:55,967 --> 00:43:57,366
Come on...

720
00:43:57,435 --> 00:44:00,202
Come on, man. Let's go, man.

721
00:44:06,243 --> 00:44:08,010
I don't believe it.

722
00:44:10,081 --> 00:44:13,482
Why? Have you forgotten what
it's like to be a human being?

723
00:44:21,559 --> 00:44:23,259
Well, Steve?

724
00:44:23,327 --> 00:44:24,793
All right.

725
00:44:24,863 --> 00:44:27,596
Yeah, I know.

726
00:44:27,665 --> 00:44:29,131
But you know what?

727
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:32,301
It felt pretty good being
on the D.A.'s side for once.

728
00:44:32,370 --> 00:44:34,303
I tell you what...

729
00:44:34,372 --> 00:44:37,973
When you get out,
let's try for a rematch.

730
00:44:38,043 --> 00:44:40,075
It's a deal.

731
00:44:51,156 --> 00:44:54,356
Tiny, Tiny, thanks
for helping me out.

732
00:44:54,425 --> 00:44:55,503
I'm glad, man.

733
00:44:55,527 --> 00:44:57,192
No, we make a hell of a team.

734
00:44:57,261 --> 00:44:58,828
When you get out, look me up.

735
00:44:58,897 --> 00:45:00,195
Here's my card.

736
00:45:02,767 --> 00:45:03,865
I don't know.

737
00:45:03,935 --> 00:45:06,001
No, I might have a job for you.

738
00:45:06,070 --> 00:45:07,990
What are you in
here for, anyway?

739
00:45:08,039 --> 00:45:09,438
Aggravated assault.

740
00:45:09,507 --> 00:45:10,906
Armed robbery.

741
00:45:10,975 --> 00:45:12,541
Grand theft auto.

742
00:45:12,610 --> 00:45:15,478
See, I used to work for a
guy who made a ton of money,

743
00:45:15,546 --> 00:45:18,380
and I asked him for a raise,
and he wouldn't give it to me.

744
00:45:18,449 --> 00:45:19,615
So I beat him up.

745
00:45:19,684 --> 00:45:21,217
I took his gun.

746
00:45:21,286 --> 00:45:22,463
I robbed.

747
00:45:22,487 --> 00:45:25,588
I know it's wrong, but
it made me so mad.

748
00:45:26,657 --> 00:45:28,724
One thing I hate...

749
00:45:28,793 --> 00:45:30,158
is a cheapskate.

750
00:45:35,366 --> 00:45:37,232
It was just a thought.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
